{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>וַיִּחַד יִתְרוֹ.</b> And Jethro rejoiced — this is its plain sense. And a midrash aggadah: his flesh broke out in prickles upon prickles — he was grieved over the destruction of Egypt. That is what people say: 'A convert, even up to ten generations — do not mock an Aramean in his face.'" "<b>עַל כָּל הַטּוֹבָה.</b> The good of the manna, and the well, and the Torah — and over all of them <b>אֲשֶׁר הִצִּילוֹ מִיַּד מִצְרָיִם;</b> until now no slave could flee from Egypt, for the land was locked — and these went out, sixty myriad (Mekhilta)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:58.032820563Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}